<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25943" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lassesco</span></b> , ĕre, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. inch. n.</i>
			[lassus], <i>to become tired, to grow weary</i>
			(post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ne lassescat fortuna,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					7, 40, 41, § 130</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">14, 2, 4,
				§ 33</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">victo lassescere visu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. in Symm. 2, 101</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lassescere sub lorica,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. 22, 39</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">non bibet aquam et lassescet,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Isa. 44, 12</span></i>
			.</div>
